The solution involves determining the optimal number of buns to sell at a modified price to maximize profit. If the modified price of the first bun `b` is less than or equal to the usual price `a`, it is optimal to sell all buns at the usual price. Otherwise, the optimal number of buns to sell at the modified price `k` is the minimum of `n` and `b - a + 1`. The profit is calculated as the sum of the first `k` modified prices plus the usual price for the remaining `n - k` buns.

